## Remote Provider

The configured provider URL is `{{ remote_url }}`. The available CLI is `{{ tools }}`.{% if mcp_available %} The available fixed MCP server and tool prefix is `{{ mcp_id }}`.{% else %} No MCP server is available for this provider; use the CLI.{% endif %} The configured CLI credential environment-variable name is `{{ token_env }}`. Never read, print, log, persist, request, or pass its value in command arguments. Harnessctl does not log in, accept credentials, install a CLI, or choose a repository.

Confirm the intended provider, repository or project, issue, operation, authentication, and required capability before acting. Ambiguous context blocks mutation. Enumerate every valid issue capability exposed by installed `{{ tools }}` help{% if mcp_available %} and every live `{{ mcp_id }}` tool schema{% endif %}: create, list or search, view, update, comment or note, close, reopen, label, assign, link relationships, and manage hierarchy or issue types where the selected tool exposes them. Never infer a capability missing from help or a live schema. Never invent commands, flags, tool names, fields, or provider behavior.

For each operation, choose either `{{ tools }}`{% if mcp_available %} or one exact live `{{ mcp_id }}` tool{% endif %} based on verified repository context, authentication, and required capability. Neither route has priority. Choose before mutation; after mutation begins, do not switch routes. Missing authentication, repository context, or issue capability stops.

Remote issue titles must use the hierarchy prefix: 🚀 Initiative, 🏔️ Epic, 📖 Story, 🛠️ Task, or 🐛 Bug. Represent hierarchy through issue links and body text. Do not require labels; use only operator-established repository conventions.

